  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Senior UK rabbis come out in support of sanctions on Israeli settlements",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/09/senior-uk-rabbis-come-out-in-support-of-sanctions-on-israeli-settlements",
      "description": "<p>Spiritual leaders stress diversity of views within Jewish community and warn against inaction on settler violence</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/09/israelis-welcome-uk-sanctions-on-settlements-palestine-west-bank\">‘It’s a good start’: prominent Israelis welcome UK sanctions</a></p></li></ul><p>Prominent British rabbis have backed Ed Miliband’s sanctions on Israeli settlements, warning that the time for inaction on settler violence must come to an end.</p><p>The intervention comes after the UK’s chief rabbi, the spiritual leader of mainstream Orthodox Jews in the UK, Sir Ephraim Mirvis, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/09/ed-miliband-rejects-chief-rabbi-claim-west-bank-sanctions-british-jews-less-safe\">described UK sanctions</a> against illegal Israeli settlements in the occupied Palestinian territories as a “dark day for British Jews” and warned they could embolden people who “use hatred as a weapon against Jews”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/09/senior-uk-rabbis-come-out-in-support-of-sanctions-on-israeli-settlements\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-09T17:57:14"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘It’s a good start’: prominent Israelis welcome UK sanctions on illegal settlements",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/09/israelis-welcome-uk-sanctions-on-settlements-palestine-west-bank",
      "description": "<p>Ed Miliband’s intervention was ‘inevitable’ after Israeli government and security failures, say former ministers and diplomats</p><p>Prominent Israelis have welcomed <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing\">new UK sanctions</a> as a necessary response to settlement expansion and spiralling violence in the occupied West Bank.</p><p>The intervention was described – by the president of the Israel Academy of Sciences and Humanities, a former prime minister, an ex-head of the army and former ministers and diplomats – as an “inevitable consequence” of Israeli government and security failures.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/09/israelis-welcome-uk-sanctions-on-settlements-palestine-west-bank\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-09T17:36:42"
    },
    {
      "title": "Israel sanctions will not hurt intelligence sharing between spy agencies, says Miliband",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/09/israel-sanctions-will-not-hurt-intelligence-sharing-between-spy-agencies-says-miliband",
      "description": "<p>UK foreign secretary says international community including US shares ‘frustration’ at Israel’s failure to constrain illegal settlers</p><p>British intelligence has been given assurances by its Israeli counterpart that information sharing with the UK will continue as before, Ed Miliband, the foreign secretary, has said.</p><p>The disclosure counters predictions that his <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing\">decision to impose a ban on trade with illegal Israeli settlements</a> would lead to a collapse in cooperation between the agencies.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/09/israel-sanctions-will-not-hurt-intelligence-sharing-between-spy-agencies-says-miliband\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-09T16:14:41"
    },
